# ── Noesis workspaces ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A workspace is an append-only journal plus a review log, and it holds the
# owner's actual personal facts — including everything the spec classifies as
# `sensitive` (health, finances, identity history). Committing one would publish
# exactly the data §3.3.1 exists to keep on the device, so the two filenames the
# CLI writes are ignored wherever they appear.
journal.jsonl
reviews.jsonl
.noesis/

# ── sbt ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# sbt 2 puts all build output under target/out/.
target/
project/target/
project/project/

# ── Scala tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.bsp/
.bloop/
.metals/
.scala-build/
# Written by Metals when it configures the build; not part of the build itself.
project/metals.sbt

# ── nix ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build result symlinks. flake.lock is deliberately NOT ignored — it pins the
# toolchain and belongs in version control.
result
result-*
# direnv's cache. An .envrc, if one is added, should stay tracked.
.direnv/

# ── JVM crash artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log
core.*

# ── Editors and OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
